/**
 * The cupola, generated rather than hand-drawn.
 *
 * Seven panes in a 1000-unit square: one round at the centre and six
 * trapezoids on a 60-degree pitch around it, which is the ISS
 * observation module's actual arrangement.
 *
 * Every curve is a chord run, not an SVG arc. Fourteen segments is
 * past the point where the eye can tell at any size this renders at,
 * and it sidesteps the arc command's sweep and large-arc flags, which
 * are the usual way a shape like this comes out inside out.
 *
 * The hardware is deliberately uneven. Six identical stations with
 * evenly spaced rivets is the loudest possible signal that something
 * was drawn, so each mullion carries a different set of boxes, only
 * three of them have handrails, the cable runs hop between arbitrary
 * pairs, and every rivet is jittered in position, size and opacity.
 */

